
# Day 43: Check Identical Binary Trees

## Problem
Check whether two binary trees have the same structure and node values.

## Approach
1. If both nodes are None, return True.
2. If only one node is None, return False.
3. If their values differ, return False.
4. Recursively compare their left subtrees.
5. Recursively compare their right subtrees.
6. Return True only if both subtrees match.

## Example
Both trees contain the values 1, 2, and 3 in the same structure.

## Output
Are trees identical: True

## Time Complexity
O(n), where n is the number of nodes when the trees have matching structure.

## Space Complexity
O(h), where h is the maximum tree height, due to recursion.

## Key Learning
Two binary trees are identical only when their structures and corresponding node values match.
